{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794868250959,"sessionID":"ses_e1984dae4ffewGkE5pBa89LndO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e67c054a001zJGt8BQTyAplX6","sessionID":"ses_e1984dae4ffewGkE5pBa89LndO","messageID":"msg_1e67bebe3001a7ry2l3osSh3j7","type":"tool","id":"call_c2a6ef46041d479d9695a9e2","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-13/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-13/iterations/iteration-002.md, lines 1-87\n1: # Review Iteration 002\n2: \n3: ## Dispatcher\n4: \n5: - Mode: review, lineage `data-13`, iteration 2 of 8.\n6: - Declared target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\n7: - Area: `data`; scope files are the graph metadata, the CL-009 playbook and ADR-001.\n8: - Dimensions this iteration: security and maintainability, with the cross-scorer contract checked under maintainability.\n9: - Operator review focus binding: `review_brief-13.txt` asks for four things in this area -- the seven phrases must not pull ordinary prompts to the advisor, the playbook prompt must match its expected lines, ADR-001 must keep P05 on `/doctor:helper`, and no tune/fix/report path may read holdout rows. Iteration 1 answered the first three; this iteration closes the holdout question and the two remaining dimensions.\n10: \n11: ## Files Reviewed\n12: \n13: - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:96-110` (signal list, re-read for control characters and duplication)\n14: - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/brief-command-policy-word.md:60-198` (command blocks, expected signals, failure triage, source metadata)\n15: - `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/decision-record.md:30-38`\n16: - `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/scratch/probes.json:79-135`\n17: - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts:30-200` (whole contract, including the cross-scorer case)\n18: - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py:4200-4215` (intent signal phrase reader)\n19: - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs:1-60,240-260,1230-1390` (input surfaces, no corpus read)\n20: - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs:20-130` (holdout refusal, read as the named hygiene surface)\n21: - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json` (signal map, re-read)\n22: - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:196` (catalog row for CL-009)\n23: - `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-13/deep-review-findings-registry.json` (reduced state)\n24: - `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-13/deep-review-strategy.md` (reduced state)\n25: \n26: ## Findings - New\n27: \n28: ### P0 Findings\n29: \n30: None.\n31: \n32: ### P1 Findings\n33: \n34: None new. F001 from iteration 1 remains active: the new signals are indexed as ordinary words in the native lexical lane.\n35: \n36: ### P2 Findings\n37: \n38: 1. **The declared-phrase contract holds in one scorer and not the other** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts:169-200` -- The specificity test asserts cross-scorer parity for exact declared phrases, but after the seven-signal addition the two shipped scorers disagree on an ordinary sense of one of them. `the arena is clean now` returns `system-skill-advisor` at 0.82 in the native scorer and no skill at all in the Python fallback; `clean arena seating chart for the stadium` puts the advisor first natively and `sk-design` first in Python. The test's cross-scorer case still covers only `browser agent` and `css extraction`, so this class is unpinned.\n39:    Finding class: test-coverage\n40:    Scope proof: Ran the Python fallback in-process with the committed `skill-graph.json` signals and no SQLite graph, and compared its top-1 with the native `scoreAdvisorPrompt` top-1 for the same prompt set; the divergence reproduces on both prompts and disappears for the two phrases the test already pins.\n41:    Affected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json`\n42:    Case: `the arena is clean now`\n43:    Recommendation: add the ordinary-sense prompts as cross-scorer fixtures once the phrase-scoring fix lands, so both scorers agree on what a declared phrase means.\n44: \n45: No P0 candidates. The P2 is a coverage gap rather than a behavior claim, so it needed no Hunter/Skeptic/Referee pass.\n46: \n47: ## Traceability Checks\n48: \n49: - `skill_agent` -- pass. `graph-metadata.json:101-107` and the compiled `skill-graph.json` signal map carry the identical seven strings; the projection reads 61 skills from SQLite and exposes the same `intentSignals` list.\n50: - `agent_cross_runtime` -- not applicable (`applicable: false`). This area defines no agent file; the only runtime-specific artifact is the Claude hook the CL-009 playbook drives, and that hook is unchanged by the diff.\n51: - `playbook_capability` -- pass. The parent and child labels were reproduced with `renderAdvisorBrief` from the committed row: `system-skilled-doctor → /doctor:update (ask)` and `(parent-named only)`, matching `brief-command-policy-word.md:148` and `:160-161`.\n52: \n53: ## Integration Evidence\n54: \n55: - Holdout hygiene: `derive-command-bridges.cjs` reads route YAML, skill frontmatter and the two scorer sources (lines 251, 539, 1247-1249); it never opens `command-prompts.jsonl`, `holdout-prompts.jsonl` or `behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl`. `measure-brief-cost.mjs:124` refuses a holdout row before spawning. No tune, fix or report path in this area reads a holdout row.\n56: - Playbook: the six hook invocations use `mktemp -d` state directories and literal JSON payloads; the changed lines add no credential, token or environment dump. `rm -rf \"$T\"` runs on the mktemp path only.\n57: - ADR: `decision-record.md:37` and `acceptance-criteria.md:59` still describe P05's helper ranking; `probes.json` P05 row agrees at 0.8.\n58: \n59: ## Edge Cases\n60: \n61: - The Python fallback has no command-bridge layer, so P05 there returns `system-skill-advisor` rather than `command-doctor-helper`. This is a scorer-scope difference, not a contradiction of ADR-001, which names a command-level helper route; it is recorded so a later reader does not treat the fallback result as a regression.\n62: - The seven signals are unique in the file (39 entries, 0 duplicates) and contain no control characters, backticks, `$` or backslashes, so they cannot alter the JSON or inject shell text.\n63: - `manual-testing-playbook.md:196` carries only the CL-009 title and link, so the feature-file version bump needs no catalog edit.\n64: \n65: ## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n66: \n67: - Security: the signal addition is static author data read by substring and token checks, with no prompt-built regular expression, no filesystem read, no network call and no credential surface. The playbook's temp handling and the bridge generator's inputs are clean for this change.\n68: - Maintainability: the CL-009 feature version bumped `1.0.1.0 -> 1.0.2.0`, all three prompt occurrences and the Expected block agree, and the failure triage still names the two render tests that exist.\n69: - The reducer-owned state is coherent: two open findings, correctness and traceability covered, security and maintainability marked here.\n70: \n71: ## Ruled Out\n72: \n73: - A holdout leak through command-bridge generation: the generator's input list has no corpus path.\n74: - A secret or environment exposure in the playbook's changed blocks: the payloads carry a prompt, cwd, hook event name and session id only.\n75: - A JSON or shell injection through a signal string: every entry is plain lowercase text with no metacharacter.\n76: - A duplicate-signal amplification: the file has no duplicate intent signal.\n77: \n78: ## Next Focus\n79: \n80: - Dimension: all four re-verified (convergence pass).\n81: - Focus area: re-run the F001 and F003 cases from the final tree, confirm the registry and strategy agree with the iteration records, and take the stop decision.\n82: - Reason: correctness, traceability, security and maintainability all have evidence; the only open question is whether the run may stop.\n83: - Rotation status: security and maintainability complete; no new dimension remains.\n84: - Blocked/productive carry-forward: F001 is the only active P1 and stays open; F002 and F003 are P2.\n85: - Required evidence: a reproduction run and a convergence decision naming any blocker.\n86: \n87: Review verdict: CONDITIONAL","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-13/iterations/iteration-002.md, lines 1-87\n1: # Review Iteration 002\n2: \n3: ## Dispatcher\n4: \n5: - Mode: review, lineage `data-13`, iteration 2 of 8.\n6: - Declared target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\n7: - Area: `data`; scope files are the graph metadata, the CL-009 playbook and ADR-001.\n8: - Dimensions this iteration: security and maintainability, with the cross-scorer contract checked under maintainability.\n9: - Operator revi