{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794868494190,"sessionID":"ses_e1984dae4ffewGkE5pBa89LndO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e67fbe21001rMb5L2axaCUXYV","sessionID":"ses_e1984dae4ffewGkE5pBa89LndO","messageID":"msg_1e67fae86001mMGerRYAx67Yi1","type":"tool","id":"call_bac85a50325346e29f340b38","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md, lines 1-29\n1: # Review Report: Command Surfacing Build, Pass Thirteen (two lineages)\n2: \n3: - Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\n4: - Pass: the thirteenth review pass, over phase 040's build `b8ebee37d75..932aff4e437` (`review/review-scope-13.txt`), run under the operator's full-loop answer.\n5: - Executor: `cli-opencode` with `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at reasoning effort max, cap eight iterations each, threshold 0.10, stop policy convergence, through `fanout-run.cjs` (exit 0). Brief `review/review-brief-13.txt`, config `review/deep-review-fanout-config-pass-13.json`. Pass twelve's report is kept as `review-report-pass-12.md`.\n6: \n7: ## 1. Executive Summary\n8: \n9: - **Verdict: CONDITIONAL, all three P1 fixed.** P0 0, P1 3, P2 7. The fixes are in phase 040 and pass fourteen reads them.\n10: - **Stop.** data-13 stopped at iteration 3 with `converged`. mention-13 stopped at iteration 8 with `maxIterationsReached`, which is not convergence.\n11: \n12: ## 2. Findings and Dispositions\n13: \n14: | Id | Severity | Location | Finding | Disposition |\n15: |----|----------|----------|---------|-------------|\n16: | mention-13 F001 | P1 | `lib/command-attach.ts` | A document naming returned a mention before a later \"then run it\" was read | Fixed: the request clause is read first, and a naming followed by \"then\" is not only a read; two cases fail on the old code |\n17: | mention-13 F002 | P1 | `lib/command-attach.ts` | \"don't run it twice\" and \"never run it without a budget\" read as refusals | Fixed: the refusal has to end its clause; two cases fail on the old code |\n18: | data-13 F001 | P1 | advisor `graph-metadata.json` | The new phrases put clean, arena, arm and briefs into the lexical lane, so ordinary prompts topped the advisor | Fixed: six of the seven phrases removed, only \"vibe prompt hook\" kept; the five ordinary prompts no longer top the advisor; P08 and P09 declined in ADR-001 |\n19: | mention-13 F007 | P2 | `lib/command-attach.ts` comment | The fold comment broke mid-sentence | Fixed |\n20: | mention-13 F003 | P2 | `lib/command-attach.ts:441` | A markdown link label abutting its target stops being an occurrence | Open, recorded |\n21: | mention-13 F004 | P2 | `lib/command-attach.ts:459` | The post-name reader covers one clause shape | Open, recorded |\n22: | mention-13 F005 | P2 | 040 `spec.md` | The document bullet is wider than the determiner rule | Open, recorded |\n23: | mention-13 F006 | P2 | 040 `tasks.md` | CHK-FIX-002 claims matrix coverage for leads it never wraps | Open, recorded |\n24: | data-13 F002 | P2 | advisor `graph-metadata.json` | \"clean arena\" fired inside a longer noun phrase | Fixed with data-13 F001 |\n25: | data-13 F003 | P2 | `declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts` | The declared-phrase contract holds in one scorer and not the other | Open, recorded |\n26: \n27: ## 3. Verification\n28: \n29: `040-final-alignment-loop/scratch/after-pass-13.txt`: build and typecheck exit 0, stored sets unchanged, graph freshness exit 0, suite 2385 passed 0 failed with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset and set, FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5], probes 11 of 15 (P05, P08 and P09 declined in ADR-001, P04 overturned by the run's critic), and none of the five ordinary prompts tops the advisor.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md, lines 1-29\n1: # Review Report: Command Surfacing Build, Pass Thirteen (two lineages)\n2: \n3: - Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\n4: - Pass: the thirteenth review pass, over phase 040's build `b8ebee37d75..932aff4e437` (`review/review-scope-13.txt`), run under the operator's full-loop answer.\n5: - Executor: `cli-opencode` with `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at reasoning effort max, cap eight iterations each, threshold 0.10, stop policy convergence, through `fanout-run.cjs` (exit 0). Brief `review/review-brief-13.txt`, config `review/deep-review-fanout-config-pass-13.json`. Pass twelve's report is kept as `review-report-pass-12.md`.\n6: \n7: ## 1. Executive Summary\n8: \n9: - **Verdict: CONDITIONAL, all three P1 fixed.** P0 0, P1 3, P2 7. The fixes are in phase 040 and pass fourteen reads them.\n10: - **Stop.** data-13 stopped at iteration 3 with `converged`. mention-13 stopped at iteration 8 with `maxIterationsReached`, which is not convergence.\n11: \n12: ## 2. Findings and Dispositions\n13: \n14: | Id | Severity | Location | Finding | Disposition |\n15: |----|----------|----------|---------|-------------|\n16: | mention-13 F001 | P1 | `lib/command-attach.ts` | A document naming returned a mention before a later \"then run it\" was read | Fixed: the request clause is read first, and a naming followed by \"then\" is not only a read; two cases fail on the old code |\n17: | mention-13 F002 | P1 | `lib/command-attach.ts` | \"don't run it twice\" and \"never run it without a budget\" read as refusals | Fixed: the refusal has to end its clause; two cases fail on the old code |\n18: | data-13 F001 | P1 | advisor `graph-metadata.json` | The new phrases put clean, arena, arm and briefs into the lexical lane, so ordinary prompts topped the advisor | Fixed: six of the seven phrases removed, only \"vibe prompt hook\" kept; the five ordinary prompts no longer top the advisor; P08 and P09 declined in ADR-001 |\n19: | mention-13 F007 | P2 | `lib/command-attach.ts` comment | The fold comment broke mid-sentence | Fixed |\n20: | mention-13 F003 | P2 | `lib/command-attach.ts:441` | A markdown link label abutting its target stops being an occurrence | Open, recorded |\n21: | mention-13 F004 | P2 | `lib/command-attach.ts:459` | The post-name reader covers one clause shape | Open, recorded |\n22: | mention-13 F005 | P2 | 040 `spec.md` | The document bullet is wider than the determiner rule | Open, recorded |\n23: | mention-13 F006 | P2 | 040 `tasks.md` | CHK-FIX-002 claims matrix coverage for leads it never wraps | Open, recorded |\n24: | data-13 F002 | P2 | advisor `graph-metadata.json` | \"clean arena\" fired inside a longer noun phrase | Fixed with data-13 F001 |\n25: | data-13 F003 | P2 | `declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts` | The declared-phrase contract holds in one scorer and not the other | Open, recorded |\n26: \n27: ## 3. Verification\n28: \n29: `040-final-alignment-loop/scratch/after-pass-13.txt`: build and typecheck exit 0, stored sets unchanged, graph freshness exit 0, suite 2385 passed 0 failed with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset and set, FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5], probes 11 of 15 (P05, P08 and P09 declined in ADR-001, P04 overturned by the run's critic), and none of the five ordinary prompts tops the advisor."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794868493857,"end":1794868494190}}}}
