{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794868784894,"sessionID":"ses_e1984dae4ffewGkE5pBa89LndO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e6841bc50023FTcp7HmT99e8y","sessionID":"ses_e1984dae4ffewGkE5pBa89LndO","messageID":"msg_1e6840be7001XmoHCevyOzaUxV","type":"tool","id":"call_13d5297a01b3413b81faf428","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n| correctness | CONDITIONAL | 1 | Four ordinary prompts top the advisor through remaining generic signals (F001) |\n| traceability | CONDITIONAL | 1 | ADR-001 and the probe rows agree; the T008 evidence sentence is wider than its five-prompt check (F001) |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\n- P1 (Required): 1\n- P2 (Suggestions): 0\n- Resolved: 0\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Init: reading the scope file, both diffs, then the whole files at `e626653ce79` before choosing a focus. It separated the phrase delta (six removed, one kept) from the ADR delta (three probes declined).\n- Iteration 1: scoring the ordinary prompts in-process with the committed projection, then dropping one signal at a time. The single-signal drop test separated a real signal match from a description or graph-edge effect and gave each P1 case a causal proof.\n- Iteration 1: reproducing the pass-thirteen leak transcript first, then widening it. The reproduction showed the removed phrases are clean and the residual lives in older signals.\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Init: none.\n- Iteration 1: none. The first attempt at `doctor-helper-match.cjs` put the prompt before `--` and was rejected; the documented `--` form worked.","oldString":"## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n<!