{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794868998864,"sessionID":"ses_e1984dae4ffewGkE5pBa89LndO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e687715f002TQI7CSsp0jlQr4","sessionID":"ses_e1984dae4ffewGkE5pBa89LndO","messageID":"msg_1e68766e2001isJ12GzjVuMAUT","type":"tool","id":"call_2c2b394824a54e6985dd6de0","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-193\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Strategy - advisor intent signals and ADR-001 pass fourteen\n3: description: Runtime strategy for the data-14 lineage, tracking the six removed advisor intent signals, the one kept phrase, and ADR-001's decline of probes P05, P08 and P09.\n4: importance_tier: normal\n5: contextType: planning\n6: ---\n7: \n8: # Deep Review Strategy - data-14\n9: \n10: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n11: \n12: ### Purpose\n13: \n14: Persistent state for the `data-14` lineage of review pass fourteen. It records which dimensions remain, what was found, which approaches worked, and where the next iteration focuses.\n15: \n16: ### Usage\n17: \n18: - **Init:** populated from the review brief, the scope file and the commit range.\n19: - **Per iteration:** read Next Focus, review the named area, record findings, mark dimensions, and set the next focus.\n20: - **Mutability:** updated in place by this lineage.\n21: \n22: ---\n23: \n24: ## 2. TOPIC\n25: \n26: Review of the data area for command surfacing pass fourteen. The area covers `system-skill-advisor`'s `intent_signals` in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json`, where six phrases were removed and only \"vibe prompt hook\" remains from the seven pass thirteen appended, and ADR-001 in `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/decision-record.md`, which now declines probes P05, P08 and P09 and fixes P07 with \"vibe prompt hook\" alone. The diff runs `932aff4e437..e626653ce79`.\n27: \n28: The operator's question for this area is narrow: does any remaining intent signal pull an ordinary prompt to the advisor, and does ADR-001 stay consistent with the tree it describes.\n29: \n30: ---\n31: \n32: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n33: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n34: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n35: - [ ] security\n36: - [ ] maintainability\n37: \n38: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n39: \n40: ---\n41: \n42: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n43: \n44: - Reviewing the mention area (`command-attach.ts` and its guard tests) assigned to `mention-14`; read-only context only.\n45: - Re-reporting the recorded limits in `review-brief-14.txt` unless a new input breaks them.\n46: - Re-reporting the open P2 list of `038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/alignment-final-dispositions.md` and of review passes ten to thirteen.\n47: - Running the repository suite, the build, or any git write; this lineage reports only.\n48: - Opening `command-prompts.jsonl`, `holdout-prompts.jsonl` or `behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl` except through the allowed aggregate path; the holdout rule stays in force.\n49: \n50: ---\n51: \n52: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n53: \n54: - Composite convergence stop at threshold 0.10 with all four dimensions covered.\n55: - `maxIterations` 8 reached without a legal convergence stop.\n56: - A blocking stop from `convergence.cjs` naming an uncovered dimension or an unresolved active P0.\n57: \n58: ---\n59: \n60: ## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n61: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n62: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n63: - [x] correctness\n64: - [x] traceability\n65: \n66: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n71: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n72: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n73: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n74: - P1 (Required): 1\n75: - P2 (Suggestions): 0\n76: - Resolved: 0\n77: \n78: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n83: \n84: - Init: reading the scope file, both diffs, then the whole files at `e626653ce79` before choosing a focus. It separated the phrase delta (six removed, one kept) from the ADR delta (three probes declined).\n85: - Iteration 1: scoring the ordinary prompts in-process with the committed projection, then dropping one signal at a time. The single-signal drop test separated a real signal match from a description or graph-edge effect and gave each P1 case a causal proof.\n86: - Iteration 1: reproducing the pass-thirteen leak transcript first, then widening it. The reproduction showed the removed phrases are clean and the residual lives in older signals.\n87: \n88: ---\n89: \n90: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n91: \n92: - Init: none.\n93: - Iteration 1: none. The first attempt at `doctor-helper-match.cjs` put the prompt before `--` and was rejected; the documented `--` form worked.\n94: \n95: ---\n96: \n97: ## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n98: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n99: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n100: ### A broken ADR-to-probe linkage: P05's helper ranking, P07's pass and the P08/P09 non-advisor outcomes all reproduce. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n101: - What was tried: A broken ADR-to-probe linkage: P05's helper ranking, P07's pass and the P08/P09 non-advisor outcomes all reproduce.\n102: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n103: - Do NOT retry: A broken ADR-to-probe linkage: P05's helper ranking, P07's pass and the P08/P09 non-advisor outcomes all reproduce.\n104: \n105: ### A regression caused by the pass-thirteen removal in the five prompts it tested: all five reproduce the pass-thirteen transcript. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n106: - What was tried: A regression caused by the pass-thirteen removal in the five prompts it tested: all five reproduce the pass-thirteen transcript.\n107: - Why bl