s lineage reports only.\n48: - Opening `command-prompts.jsonl`, `holdout-prompts.jsonl` or `behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl` except through the allowed aggregate path; the holdout rule stays in force.\n49: \n50: ---\n51: \n52: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n53: \n54: - Composite convergence stop at threshold 0.10 with all four dimensions covered.\n55: - `maxIterations` 8 reached without a legal convergence stop.\n56: - A blocking stop from `convergence.cjs` naming an uncovered dimension or an unresolved active P0.\n57: \n58: ---\n59: \n60: ## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n61: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n62: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n63: - [x] correctness\n64: - [x] traceability\n65: \n66: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n71: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n72: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n73: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n74: - P1 (Required): 1\n75: - P2 (Suggestions): 0\n76: - Resolved: 0\n77: \n78: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n83: \n84: - Init: reading the scope file, both diffs, then the whole files at `e626653ce79` before choosing a focus. It separated the phrase delta (six removed, one kept) from the ADR delta (three probes declined).\n85: - Iteration 1: scoring the ordinary prompts in-process with the committed projection, then dropping one signal at a time. The single-signal drop test separated a real signal match from a description or graph-edge effect and gave each P1 case a causal proof.\n86: - Iteration 1: reproducing the pass-thirteen leak transcript first, then widening it. The reproduction showed the removed phrases are clean and the residual lives in older signals.\n87: \n88: ---\n89: \n90: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n91: \n92: - Init: none.\n93: - Iteration 1: none. The first attempt at `doctor-helper-match.cjs` put the prompt before `--` and was rejected; the documented `--` form worked.\n94: \n95: ---\n96: \n97: ## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n98: <!-- ANCHO