{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794869081823,"sessionID":"ses_e1984dae4ffewGkE5pBa89LndO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e6888b560026q0INAd4nLRZtw","sessionID":"ses_e1984dae4ffewGkE5pBa89LndO","messageID":"msg_1e6887b30001bKtUELRGtrVUzf","type":"tool","id":"call_74cf9490720341868cddef31","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 003\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, lineage `data-14`, iteration 3 of 8.\n- Declared target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\n- Area: `data`; scope files are the advisor graph metadata and ADR-001 in the 040 decision record.\n- Dimensions this iteration: all four re-verified for the convergence pass (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability).\n- Operator review focus binding: `review-brief-14.txt` asks whether any remaining advisor intent signal pulls an ordinary prompt to the advisor, and whether ADR-001 stays consistent. This iteration re-runs both checks from the final tree, confirms the two open findings still reproduce, and takes the stop decision.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:66-100` (final signal list, re-read)\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/decision-record.md:37` (ADR-001, re-read)\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/scratch/probes.json` (P05/P07/P08/P09 rows, re-read)\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/scratch/after-pass-13.txt:16-20` (five-prompt leak check, re-read)\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/deep-review-findings-registry.json` (reduced state)\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/deep-review-strategy.md` (reduced state)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. F001 remains active: four ordinary prompts still top the advisor through the remaining generic signals, and each single-signal drop removes the advisor top-1.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new. F002 remains open: ADR-001 does not record the residual leak and no test pins the remaining generic signals.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code` -- pass, re-verified. P05 still returns `command-doctor-helper` with `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` ranked first by `doctor-helper-match.cjs`; P07 returns `system-skill-advisor`; P08 returns `sk-doc`; P09 returns no skill. ADR-001 and the probe rows agree on all four.\n- `checklist_evidence` -- partial. AC-004's waived status and ADR-001 agree; T008's \"no ordinary prompt tops the advisor\" sentence remains wider than the five-prompt transcript it cites, and F001 is the counterexample. The partial is stable across iterations 1 and 3, not new.\n- `skill_agent` -- pass, re-verified. The committed projection still lists 33 canonical advisor signals and none of the six removed phrases.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- Final-tree replay of the pass-thirteen leak check: the five transcripts still match (`the routing arm of the load balancer is flaky`, `the advisor briefs me every morning`, `the arena is clean now` and `clean the routing table` return no skill; `fix the routing arm in the nginx config` returns `system-spec-kit`).\n- Final-tree replay of F001: the four ordinary prompts still return `system-skill-advisor` at 0.82. The finding is unchanged, so the stop cannot read as clean.\n- Registry and strategy agree with the iteration records: two open findings (one P1, one P2), all four dimensions covered.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The four F001 prompts pre-date the pass-thirteen change, so the finding is a residual limit rather than a regression. It still gates the verdict because the operator's own ADR applies the ordinary-prompt standard.\n- The advisor returns 0.82 on all four because its score is floored; the lane evidence and the drop tests, not the confidence value, carry the finding.\n- P08 and P09 remain declined in ADR-001. Their non-advisor routing is expected, not a new defect.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The six removed phrases are absent from both the author file and the committed projection.\n- `vibe prompt hook` remains advisor-specific; P07 still passes with it alone.\n- Security: both scope files remain static author text and markdown with no secret, trust boundary or holdout reference.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A changed outcome since iteration 1: the F001 and pass-thirteen transcripts reproduce exactly.\n- A state disagreement between the registry and the iteration records: both list the same two open findings and four covered dimensions.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none remaining; synthesis.\n- Focus area: write the review report from the registry, with F001 as the active P1 and F002 as the P2 advisory, and keep the verdict CONDITIONAL.\n- Reason: all four dimensions are covered and the stop decision is legal on coverage; the active P1 keeps the verdict below PASS.\n- Rotation status: complete.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: F001 and F002 stay open; no new direction remains.\n- Required evidence: the convergence decision and the synthesis report.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 003\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, lineage `data-14`, iteration 3 of 8.\\n- Declared target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\\n- Area: `data`; scope files are the advisor graph metadata and ADR-001 in the 040 decision record.\\n- Dimensions this iteration: all four re-verified for the convergence pass (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability).\\n- Operator review focus binding: `review-brief-14.txt` asks whether any remaining advisor intent signal pulls an ordinary prompt to the advisor, and whether ADR-001 stays consistent. This iteration re-runs both checks from the final tree, confirms the two open findings still reproduce, and takes the stop decision.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:66-100` (final signal list, re-read)\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/decision-record.md:37` (ADR-001, re-read)\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/scratch/probes.json` (P05/P07/P08/P09 rows, re-read)\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/scratch/after-pass-13.txt:16-20` (five-prompt leak check, re-read)\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/deep-review-findings-registry.json` (reduced state)\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/deep-review-strategy.md` (reduced state)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. F001 remains active: four ordinary prompts still top the advisor through the remaining generic signals, and each single-signal drop removes the advisor top-1.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new. F002 remains open: ADR-001 does not record the residual leak and no test pins the remaining generic signals.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code` -- pass, re-verified. P05 still returns `command-doctor-helper` with `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` ranked first by `doctor-helper-match.cjs`; P07 returns `system-skill-advisor`; P08 returns `sk-doc`; P09 returns no skill. ADR-001 and the probe rows agree on all four.\\n- `checklist_evidence` -- partial. AC-004's waived status and ADR-001 agree; T008's \\\"no ordinary prompt tops the advisor\\\" sentence remains wider than the five-prompt transcript it cites, and F001 is the counterexample. The partial is stable across iterations 1 and 3, not new.\\n- `skill_agent` -- pass, re-verified. The committed projection still lists 33 canonical advisor signals and none of the six removed phrases.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- Final-tree replay of the pass-thirteen leak check: the five transcripts still match (`the routing arm of the load balancer is flaky`, `the advisor briefs me every morning`, `the arena is clean now` and `clean the routing table` return no skill; `fix the routing arm in the nginx config` returns `system-spec-kit`).\\n- Final-tree replay of F001: the four ordinary prompts still return `system-skill-advisor` at 0.82. The finding is unchanged, so the stop cannot read as clean.\\n- Registry and strategy agree with the iteration records: two open findings (one P1, one P2), all four dimensions covered.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The four F001 prompts pre-date the pass-thirteen change, so the finding is a residual limit rather than a regression. It still gates the verdict because the operator's own ADR applies the ordinary-prompt standard.\\n- The advisor returns 0.82 on all four because its score is floored; the lane evidence and the drop tests, not the confidence value, carry the finding.\\n- P08 and P09 remain declined in ADR-001. Their non-advisor routing is expected, not a new defect.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The six removed phrases are absent from both the author file and the committed projection.\\n- `vibe prompt hook` remains advisor-specific; P07 still passes with it alone.\\n- Security: both scope files remain static author text and markdown with no secret, trust boundary or holdout reference.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A changed outcome since iteration 1: the F001 and pass-thirteen transcripts reproduce exactly.\\n- A state disagreement between the registry and the iteration records: both list the same two open findings and four covered dimensions.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: none remaining; synthesis.\\n- Focus area: write the review report from the registry, with F001 as the active P1 and F002 as the P2 advisory, and keep the verdict CONDITIONAL.\\n- Reason: all four dimensions are covered and the stop decision is legal on coverage; the active P1 keeps the verdict below PASS.\\n- Rotation status: complete.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: F001 and F002 stay open; no new direction remains.\\n- Required evidence: the convergence decision and the synthesis report.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794869070678,"end":1794869081823}}}}
