{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794869172198,"sessionID":"ses_e1984dae4ffewGkE5pBa89LndO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e689edbb001eoZi5jxxaYiadK","sessionID":"ses_e1984dae4ffewGkE5pBa89LndO","messageID":"msg_1e689de960010tG3eEqwsJCwVe","type":"tool","id":"call_8b24d988843940dca994fc54","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 004\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, lineage `data-14`, iteration 4 of 8.\n- Declared target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\n- Area: `data`; scope files are the advisor graph metadata and ADR-001 in the 040 decision record.\n- Dimensions this iteration: all four re-verified for the stop pass (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability).\n- Operator review focus binding: `review-brief-14.txt` asks whether any remaining advisor intent signal pulls an ordinary prompt to the advisor, and whether ADR-001 stays consistent. Iteration 3 answered both from the final tree but left `checklist_evidence` at `partial`, which the convergence gate reads as one unfinished hard protocol and one gating failure, so the stop was blocked. This iteration closes that protocol with file:line evidence and retakes the stop.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/acceptance-criteria.md:59` (AC-004 row, re-read for the protocol close)\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/tasks.md:49,58` (T006 and T008 rows, re-read)\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/scratch/probes.json` (P05/P07/P08/P09 rows, re-read)\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/decision-record.md:37` (ADR-001, re-read)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:66-100` (final signal list, re-read)\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/deep-review-findings-registry.json` (reduced state)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. F001 remains active unchanged: four ordinary prompts top the advisor through the remaining generic signals.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new. F002 remains open as the documentation and test-surface advisory.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `checklist_evidence` -- pass, raised from iteration 3's `partial`. The checklist rows that carry this area do have evidence and agree with the registry: AC-004 is Waived with ADR-001 as its carrier and describes P05, P08 and P09 as declined (`acceptance-criteria.md:59`); T006 records the original seven-phrase build (`tasks.md:49`); T008 records the six-phrase removal and the five-prompt check (`tasks.md:58`); the probe rows carry the matching P05, P07, P08 and P09 actuals (`scratch/probes.json`). F001 is the residual the five-prompt check does not cover, and it stays in the registry as an active P1 rather than being folded into this protocol's status. Evidence: `acceptance-criteria.md:59`, `tasks.md:58`, `scratch/probes.json`.\n- `spec_code` -- pass, re-verified. P05 returns `command-doctor-helper` with `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` first; P07 returns `system-skill-advisor`; P08 returns `sk-doc`; P09 returns no skill. ADR-001 and the probe rows agree on all four.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- The convergence inputs after iteration 3 named `checklist_evidence` in `unfinishedCoreProtocols` and `gatingFailures: 1`; both trace to the partial status recorded then, not to a new defect. This iteration records the protocol with its evidence and leaves F001 and F002 in the registry.\n- No new code or data change was read in this iteration that would alter F001, F002 or the probe outcomes.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- `checklist_evidence` is marked `pass` for the checklist's evidence standing, not for the advisor's ordinary-prompt behavior. The behavior defect is F001 and remains active; the verdict stays CONDITIONAL.\n- T006's seven-phrase evidence is historical and superseded by T008 and ADR-001; it is consistent as a record of the earlier action, which is why it does not force a fail here.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Both scope files are unchanged since iteration 3, and the final-tree replay still reproduces every probe outcome and both finding cases.\n- The registry holds two open findings (F001 P1, F002 P2), all four dimensions covered, and no search debt.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A new gating failure introduced since iteration 3: the only blocker was the partial protocol status, and it is closed here with evidence.\n- A changed F001 or F002 case: both reproduce unchanged.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none remaining; synthesis.\n- Focus area: write the review report from the registry, with F001 as the active P1 and F002 as the P2 advisory, and keep the verdict CONDITIONAL.\n- Reason: all four dimensions are covered, both core protocols now have terminal statuses, and the stop decision is expected to be legal.\n- Rotation status: complete.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: F001 and F002 stay open; no new direction remains.\n- Required evidence: the convergence STOP decision and the synthesis report.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/iterations/iteration-004.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/iterations/iteration-004.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/iterations/iteration-004.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 004\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, lineage `data-14`, iteration 4 of 8.\\n- Declared target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\\n- Area: `data`; scope files are the advisor graph metadata and ADR-001 in the 040 decision record.\\n- Dimensions this iteration: all four re-verified for the stop pass (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability).\\n- Operator review focus binding: `review-brief-14.txt` asks whether any remaining advisor intent signal pulls an ordinary prompt to the advisor, and whether ADR-001 stays consistent. Iteration 3 answered both from the final tree but left `checklist_evidence` at `partial`, which the convergence gate reads as one unfinished hard protocol and one gating failure, so the stop was blocked. This iteration closes that protocol with file:line evidence and retakes the stop.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/acceptance-criteria.md:59` (AC-004 row, re-read for the protocol close)\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/tasks.md:49,58` (T006 and T008 rows, re-read)\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/scratch/probes.json` (P05/P07/P08/P09 rows, re-read)\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/decision-record.md:37` (ADR-001, re-read)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:66-100` (final signal list, re-read)\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/deep-review-findings-registry.json` (reduced state)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. F001 remains active unchanged: four ordinary prompts top the advisor through the remaining generic signals.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new. F002 remains open as the documentation and test-surface advisory.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `checklist_evidence` -- pass, raised from iteration 3's `partial`. The checklist rows that carry this area do have evidence and agree with the registry: AC-004 is Waived with ADR-001 as its carrier and describes P05, P08 and P09 as declined (`acceptance-criteria.md:59`); T006 records the original seven-phrase build (`tasks.md:49`); T008 records the six-phrase removal and the five-prompt check (`tasks.md:58`); the probe rows carry the matching P05, P07, P08 and P09 actuals (`scratch/probes.json`). F001 is the residual the five-prompt check does not cover, and it stays in the registry as an active P1 rather than being folded into this protocol's status. Evidence: `acceptance-criteria.md:59`, `tasks.md:58`, `scratch/probes.json`.\\n- `spec_code` -- pass, re-verified. P05 returns `command-doctor-helper` with `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` first; P07 returns `system-skill-advisor`; P08 returns `sk-doc`; P09 returns no skill. ADR-001 and the probe rows agree on all four.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- The convergence inputs after iteration 3 named `checklist_evidence` in `unfinishedCoreProtocols` and `gatingFailures: 1`; both trace to the partial status recorded then, not to a new defect. This iteration records the protocol with its evidence and leaves F001 and F002 in the registry.\\n- No new code or data change was read in this iteration that would alter F001, F002 or the probe outcomes.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- `checklist_evidence` is marked `pass` for the checklist's evidence standing, not for the advisor's ordinary-prompt behavior. The behavior defect is F001 and remains active; the verdict stays CONDITIONAL.\\n- T006's seven-phrase evidence is historical and superseded by T008 and ADR-001; it is consistent as a record of the earlier action, which is why it does not force a fail here.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- Both scope files are unchanged since iteration 3, and the final-tree replay still reproduces every probe outcome and both finding cases.\\n- The registry holds two open findings (F001 P1, F002 P2), all four dimensions covered, and no search debt.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A new gating failure introduced since iteration 3: the only blocker was the partial protocol status, and it is closed here with evidence.\\n- A changed F001 or F002 case: both reproduce unchanged.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: none remaining; synthesis.\\n- Focus area: write the review report from the registry, with F001 as the active P1 and F002 as the P2 advisory, and keep the verdict CONDITIONAL.\\n- Reason: all four dimensions are covered, both core protocols now have terminal statuses, and the stop decision is expected to be legal.\\n- Rotation status: complete.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: F001 and F002 stay open; no new direction remains.\\n- Required evidence: the convergence STOP decision and the synthesis report.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/iterations/iteration-004.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794869161403,"end":1794869172198}}}}
