{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794869389979,"sessionID":"ses_e1984dae4ffewGkE5pBa89LndO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e68d37d90019bmip8aV45H5Gy","sessionID":"ses_e1984dae4ffewGkE5pBa89LndO","messageID":"msg_1e68d268a001EtvAmPOJsVq6Ix","type":"tool","id":"call_54960507a47e479ca34f93ea","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 005\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, lineage `data-14`, iteration 5 of 8.\n- Declared target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\n- Area: `data`; scope files are the advisor graph metadata and ADR-001 in the 040 decision record.\n- Dimensions this iteration: correctness and maintainability, the recovery target and the record surface.\n- Operator review focus binding: `review-brief-14.txt` asks whether any remaining advisor intent signal pulls an ordinary prompt to the advisor, and whether ADR-001 stays consistent. The recovery is a different granularity of the same question: instead of four hand-picked prompts, one ordinary-sense prompt per generic remaining signal.\n- Recovery cause: iteration 4's stop decision was `STUCK_RECOVERY` (`stuckThresholdReached`) after two zero-novelty passes. The recovery event is recorded in the ledger; this pass changes the approach rather than repeating the same replay.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:66-100` (each remaining signal checked against an ordinary-sense prompt)\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/decision-record.md:37` (ADR-001, re-read for the record boundary)\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/scratch/probes.json` (P05/P07/P08/P09 rows)\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/deep-review-findings-registry.json` (reduced state)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. F001 stays active with its four cases: `route request to the backend service`, `which skill should I learn next as a developer`, `measure the workflow throughput`, `not offering a skill in the job listing`.\n\nThe per-signal sweep tested a wider prompt set, and the extra prompts are inside the advisor's stated contract, so they do not extend F001:\n- `which skill should i use for this task` is a skill-selection request, which is exactly the advisor's declared job.\n- `my command transcripts are huge`, `the scorer fusion layer is slow`, `this lane fusion change needs a test`, `the local fallback scorer returns nothing`, `check the prompt hook health endpoint` and `index private skills from the vendor folder` name the advisor's own measurement, scorer, hook and private-index surfaces; routing them to the advisor is expected.\n- `the gate 2 review of the bridge failed` returns `sk-code` (0.9076), not the advisor.\n- `show me how to add a private repository`, `measure the workflow latency in production` and `the routing confidence is low on this model` return no skill.\n- `route my request through the proxy` (0.8621) and `write a prompt-time brief for the team` (0.8734) are the same generic-signal class as F001 but are ambiguous enough that they are recorded as additional cases for that finding rather than a new one. They do not change its severity.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new. F002 stays open: ADR-001 does not carry the residual leak.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code` -- pass, re-verified in the recovery pass. P05/P07/P08/P09 outcomes still match ADR-001 and the probe rows.\n- `checklist_evidence` -- pass. The checklist rows and the registry agree; F001 and F002 are recorded separately as the active findings.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- Recovery scope: the sweep covered every remaining generic signal in `graph-metadata.json:66-100`. The two additional ambiguous cases (`route my request through the proxy`, `write a prompt-time brief for the team`) reproduce through `author:route my request` and `author:prompt-time brief`, the same single-signal mechanism as F001.\n- The four F001 cases and the five pass-thirteen prompts reproduce unchanged.\n- No state disagreement: the registry holds F001 and F002, and this iteration adds no finding row.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The recovery sweep found in-domain prompts the advisor should answer. Treating them as leaks would overstate F001 and would recommend narrowing signals the advisor needs; they are recorded as within-contract examples instead.\n- `route my request through the proxy` and `write a prompt-time brief for the team` sit on the boundary. They are listed with F001's cases so a later fix can decide whether to narrow `route my request` and `prompt-time brief` too; they are not counted as a new finding.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- No signal outside the four F001 cases produces a clearly out-of-contract top-1 in the sweep.\n- Both scope files are unchanged; ADR-001 and the probe rows still agree.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A broader leak than F001 among the remaining signals: the wider sweep produced only in-domain or ambiguous results beyond the four established cases.\n- A new documentation or test-surface defect beyond F002: the ADR and test gap is unchanged from iteration 2.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none remaining; convergence check.\n- Focus area: retake the stop decision with the recovery reset in place; if it stops, synthesize with F001 as the active P1 and F002 as the P2 advisory.\n- Reason: all four dimensions are covered, both core protocols pass, and the recovery pass found no new finding.\n- Rotation status: complete.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: F001 and F002 stay open; no new direction remains.\n- Required evidence: the convergence decision and, if STOP, the synthesis report.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/iterations/iteration-005.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/iterations/iteration-005.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 005\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, lineage `data-14`, iteration 5 of 8.\\n- Declared target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\\n- Area: `data`; scope files are the advisor graph metadata and ADR-001 in the 040 decision record.\\n- Dimensions this iteration: correctness and maintainability, the recovery target and the record surface.\\n- Operator review focus binding: `review-brief-14.txt` asks whether any remaining advisor intent signal pulls an ordinary prompt to the advisor, and whether ADR-001 stays consistent. The recovery is a different granularity of the same question: instead of four hand-picked prompts, one ordinary-sense prompt per generic remaining signal.\\n- Recovery cause: iteration 4's stop decision was `STUCK_RECOVERY` (`stuckThresholdReached`) after two zero-novelty passes. The recovery event is recorded in the ledger; this pass changes the approach rather than repeating the same replay.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:66-100` (each remaining signal checked against an ordinary-sense prompt)\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/decision-record.md:37` (ADR-001, re-read for the record boundary)\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/scratch/probes.json` (P05/P07/P08/P09 rows)\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/deep-review-findings-registry.json` (reduced state)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. F001 stays active with its four cases: `route request to the backend service`, `which skill should I learn next as a developer`, `measure the workflow throughput`, `not offering a skill in the job listing`.\\n\\nThe per-signal sweep tested a wider prompt set, and the extra prompts are inside the advisor's stated contract, so they do not extend F001:\\n- `which skill should i use for this task` is a skill-selection request, which is exactly the advisor's declared job.\\n- `my command transcripts are huge`, `the scorer fusion layer is slow`, `this lane fusion change needs a test`, `the local fallback scorer returns nothing`, `check the prompt hook health endpoint` and `index private skills from the vendor folder` name the advisor's own measurement, scorer, hook and private-index surfaces; routing them to the advisor is expected.\\n- `the gate 2 review of the bridge failed` returns `sk-code` (0.9076), not the advisor.\\n- `show me how to add a private repository`, `measure the workflow latency in production` and `the routing confidence is low on this model` return no skill.\\n- `route my request through the proxy` (0.8621) and `write a prompt-time brief for the team` (0.8734) are the same generic-signal class as F001 but are ambiguous enough that they are recorded as additional cases for that finding rather than a new one. They do not change its severity.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new. F002 stays open: ADR-001 does not carry the residual leak.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code` -- pass, re-verified in the recovery pass. P05/P07/P08/P09 outcomes still match ADR-001 and the probe rows.\\n- `checklist_evidence` -- pass. The checklist rows and the registry agree; F001 and F002 are recorded separately as the active findings.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- Recovery scope: the sweep covered every remaining generic signal in `graph-metadata.json:66-100`. The two additional ambiguous cases (`route my request through the proxy`, `write a prompt-time brief for the team`) reproduce through `author:route my request` and `author:prompt-time brief`, the same single-signal mechanism as F001.\\n- The four F001 cases and the five pass-thirteen prompts reproduce unchanged.\\n- No state disagreement: the registry holds F001 and F002, and this iteration adds no finding row.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The recovery sweep found in-domain prompts the advisor should answer. Treating them as leaks would overstate F001 and would recommend narrowing signals the advisor needs; they are recorded as within-contract examples instead.\\n- `route my request through the proxy` and `write a prompt-time brief for the team` sit on the boundary. They are listed with F001's cases so a later fix can decide whether to narrow `route my request` and `prompt-time brief` too; they are not counted as a new finding.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- No signal outside the four F001 cases produces a clearly out-of-contract top-1 in the sweep.\\n- Both scope files are unchanged; ADR-001 and the probe rows still agree.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A broader leak than F001 among the remaining signals: the wider sweep produced only in-domain or ambiguous results beyond the four established cases.\\n- A new documentation or test-surface defect beyond F002: the ADR and test gap is unchanged from iteration 2.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: none remaining; convergence check.\\n- Focus area: retake the stop decision with the recovery reset in place; if it stops, synthesize with F001 as the active P1 and F002 as the P2 advisory.\\n- Reason: all four dimensions are covered, both core protocols pass, and the recovery pass found no new finding.\\n- Rotation status: complete.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: F001 and F002 stay open; no new direction remains.\\n- Required evidence: the convergence decision and, if STOP, the synthesis report.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/iterations/iteration-005.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794869376985,"end":1794869389979}}}}
