{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794869477455,"sessionID":"ses_e1984dae4ffewGkE5pBa89LndO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e68e5b26001I13ipZEJ4LJD68","sessionID":"ses_e1984dae4ffewGkE5pBa89LndO","messageID":"msg_1e68e4df0001GF50pyLiZBvE4X","type":"tool","id":"call_3de15811d31d401c81fad074","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Report: Command Surfacing Build, Pass Fourteen - data area\n\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\n- Pass: the fourteenth review pass, `data` area of `review/review-scope-14.txt`. It diffed `932aff4e437..e626653ce79` for `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json` and `040-final-alignment-loop/decision-record.md`, then read each whole file at `e626653ce79`.\n- Lineage: `data-14`, session `fanout-data-14-1794868189353-tsxtos`, five iterations, stop reason `converged` at threshold 0.10, one stuck-recovery pass, `blockedBy` empty. Brief `review/review-brief-14.txt`.\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- **Overall verdict: CONDITIONAL.** P0 0, P1 1, P2 1 -- the counts the verdict used.\n- **hasAdvisories: false.** One P2 advisory is open, but the verdict is CONDITIONAL on the active P1, so the advisory flag is not set.\n- **Operator review focus:** Review pass fourteen. First read `review/review-brief-14.txt` and follow it: it names the area by lineage label, the scope file, the graph and stop steps each iteration runs, and the holdout rule.\n- **What the change did.** Six of the seven pass-thirteen intent signals were removed; only `vibe prompt hook` remains from that set. ADR-001 now waives AC-004 for P05, P08 and P09 and keeps their routes, and fixes P07 with `vibe prompt hook` alone.\n- **What the review found.** The removal is correct and reproduces: the five prompts pass thirteen checked no longer top the advisor, and P05/P07/P08/P09 match ADR-001. It is not complete as a leak fix: four ordinary prompts still top the advisor through older generic signals, and ADR-001 does not record that residual.\n- **Stop and recovery.** Iterations 1-2 covered all four dimensions. Iteration 3's stop was blocked because `checklist_evidence` was left `partial`; iteration 4 closed it but hit the two-pass stuck threshold. A recorded recovery pass swept one ordinary-sense prompt per remaining signal, found no new out-of-contract case, and the stop then converged.\n- **Self-check outcomes.** F001 (P1) was confirmed by the full Hunter/Skeptic/Referee pass in iteration 1: each of the four prompts loses the advisor top-1 when only its matching signal is dropped. F002 (P2) was confirmed by reading ADR-001 beside the transcript it cites. No finding was downgraded or called a false positive.\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\n`/speckit:plan` is required: the verdict is CONDITIONAL on one active P1.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"triggered\": true,\n  \"verdict\": \"CONDITIONAL\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": false,\n  \"activeFindings\": [\"F001\", \"F002\"],\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-1\",\n      \"findingIds\": [\"F001\"],\n      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n      \"title\": \"Stop generic remaining intent signals from routing ordinary prompts\",\n      \"scope\": \"advisor intent_signals scoring surface: narrow which skill, route request, not offering a skill and workflow measure to advisor-specific compounds, or exclude their single tokens from the lexical lane; pin the four ordinary prompts as fixtures\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-2\",\n      \"findingIds\": [\"F002\"],\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"Record the residual leak in the decision record and pin it\",\n      \"scope\": \"ADR-001 residual row or sentence plus a real-signal ordinary-sense fixture in the specificity test\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"specSeed\": [\n    \"State that an advisor intent signal must name advisor behaviour, not a word that appears in ordinary backend, career, HR or ops text.\",\n    \"State that a leak check must cover every remaining generic signal, not only the phrases the current change added.\",\n    \"State that a declined probe whose words were removed for leaking must be rechecked against the remaining surface.\"\n  ],\n  \"planSeed\": [\n    \"Narrow which skill, route request, not offering a skill and workflow measure to advisor-specific compounds, and add the four ordinary prompts as negative fixtures.\",\n    \"Add one ADR-001 row naming the residual generic signals and the reproducing prompts, and extend the specificity test with real-signal ordinary-sense cases.\"\n  ],\n  \"findingClasses\": [\"algorithmic\", \"matrix/evidence\"],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/lexical.ts\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts\",\n    \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/decision-record.md\"\n  ],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": true\n}\n```\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n| ID | Severity | Dimension | Location | Finding | Fix recommendation | Finding class | Scope proof | Affected surface hints |\n|----|----------|-----------|----------|---------|--------------------|---------------|-------------|------------------------|\n| F001 | P1 | correctness | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:70` | Four ordinary prompts top the advisor through pre-existing generic intent signals | Narrow which skill, route request, not offering a skill and workflow measure to advisor compounds, or exclude their single tokens; pin the four prompts | algorithmic | Each prompt returns `system-skill-advisor` 0.82 with the committed projection and loses the top-1 when only its matching signal is dropped; measure then returns `sk-design` | graph metadata, lexical lane, specificity test, after-pass-13 transcript |\n| F002 | P2 | maintainability | `040-final-alignment-loop/decision-record.md:37` | ADR-001 records the pass-thirteen fix but not the residual leak it leaves open | Add a residual row naming the remaining generic signals and the four prompts, and pin them as fixtures | matrix/evidence | Read ADR-001 and the five-prompt transcript it cites; the test file pins fixture phrases only, so the residual is unpinned | decision record, tasks evidence, specificity test |\n\nImpact notes:\n\n- F001 changes the top recommendation for ordinary text: `route request to the backend service`, `which skill should I learn next as a developer`, `measure the workflow throughput` and `not offering a skill in the job listing` all lead with the advisor. No command is attached and no mutating command is offered.\n- The four prompts pre-date the pass-thirteen change. F001 is a residual of the older surface, not a regression introduced by this diff.\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\n- **WS-1 (F001).** Treat the four generic signals as phrases only, or remove their single tokens from the lexical and derived lanes. Add the four prompts as ordinary-sense fixtures so the next phrase addition cannot silently regress. This is the same class pass thirteen fixed for the newly added phrases.\n- **WS-2 (F002).** Record the residual in ADR-001 and extend the specificity test with real-signal ordinary-sense cases. The existing test builds a fixture projection and never reads the shipped signal list.\n- No code change is made in this review. Both workstreams are planning seeds.\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- An advisor intent signal names advisor behaviour, not a word that appears in ordinary backend, career, HR or ops text.\n- A leak check must cover every remaining generic signal, not only the phrases the current change added.\n- A declined probe whose words were removed for leaking must be rechecked against the remaining surface.\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- Narrow the four generic signals to advisor-specific compounds and add the four ordinary prompts as negative fixtures.\n- Add one ADR-001 row naming the residual signals and prompts, and extend the specificity test with real-signal ordinary-sense cases.\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | 5 | P05 returns `command-doctor-helper` with `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` first; P07 advisor; P08 `sk-doc`; P09 none; ADR-001 and the probe rows agree |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pass | 5 | AC-004, T006 and T008 carry evidence; F001 and F002 are the separately recorded residuals |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | 3 | Author metadata and the committed projection carry the same 33 canonical signals |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | 1 | No agent file or runtime-specific surface in this area |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | notApplicable | 2 | No feature catalog row changes in this area |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | 2 | No manual-testing playbook source in this area |\n\nAcceptance coverage: `AC_COVERAGE` is advisory only. AC-004 is waived by ADR-001 for P05, P08 and P09; AC-005 remains unmet pending this pass and the full alignment run. The advisory does not change the verdict.\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- F002 is advisory and can land with the F001 fix.\n- The two ambiguous sweep cases, `route my request through the proxy` and `write a prompt-time brief for the team`, are recorded with F001's case set rather than as a separate finding. A later fix should decide whether `route my request` and `prompt-time brief` also need narrowing.\n- T006's evidence cell records the earlier seven-phrase build. It is historical and superseded by T008 and ADR-001; no edit is requested here.\n\n## Dimension Expansion Map\n\n| Dimension | Iterations | Coverage |\n|-----------|------------|----------|\n| correctness | 1, 3, 4, 5 | complete |\n| security | 2, 3, 4 | complete |\n| traceability | 1, 3, 4, 5 | complete |\n| maintainability | 2, 3, 4, 5 | complete |\n\n## 9. Search Ledger\n\n- Ordinary-sense sweep, correctness: four out-of-contract prompts found (`route request to the backend service`, `which skill should I learn next as a developer`, `measure the workflow throughput`, `not offering a skill in the job listing`), each proven by a single-signal drop test. Result: F001.\n- Wider recovery sweep, correctness: thirteen further prompts tested; in-domain prompts (skill selection, scorer fusion, command transcripts, prompt hook health, private skills indexing, fallback scorer) route to the advisor by contract; ambiguous prompts (`route my request through the proxy`, `write a prompt-time brief for the team`) are added to F001's case set. No new finding.\n- Pass-thirteen transcript replay: five prompts reproduce the recorded outcomes; four return no skill and one returns `system-spec-kit`.\n- ADR and probe replay: P05 helper ranking, P07 pass, P08 `sk-doc`, P09 no skill. All match ADR-001.\n- Holdout hygiene: both scope files and the cited transcript were checked for corpus references; none names `command-prompts.jsonl`, `holdout-prompts.jsonl` or `behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl`. No holdout row was read.\n- Security pass: both files are static author text and markdown; 33 signals are unique, ASCII-only and metacharacter-free; no secret, host, credential or executable path.\n\n## 10. Audit Appendix\n\n- Iterations: 5. Iteration records were recorded through `append-mode-event.cjs`; the reducer refreshed the registry, dashboard and strategy after each.\n- Convergence: stop reason `converged`, `composite_converged`, all nine legal-stop gates pass, `blockedBy` empty. One `stuckRecovery` was recorded after iteration 4 and the recovery pass was iteration 5.\n- Verdict source: the findings registry (one P1, one P2). The iteration final lines are the leaf self-report; this report and the registry agree.\n- Writes: confined to `review/lineages/data-14`. Review targets were read-only.\n- Completion line: `FANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:data-14`.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Report: Command Surfacing Build, Pass Fourteen - data area\\n\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\\n- Pass: the fourteenth review pass, `data` area of `review/review-scope-14.txt`. It diffed `932aff4e437..e626653ce79` for `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json` and `040-final-alignment-loop/decision-record.md`, then read each whole file at `e626653ce79`.\\n- Lineage: `data-14`, session `fanout-data-14-1794868189353-tsxtos`, five iterations, stop reason `converged` at threshold 0.10, one stuck-recovery pass, `blockedBy` empty. Brief `review/review-brief-14.txt`.\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n- **Overall verdict: CONDITIONAL.** P0 0, P1 1, P2 1 -- the counts the verdict used.\\n- **hasAdvisories: false.** One P2 advisory is open, but the verdict is CONDITIONAL on the active P1, so the advisory flag is not set.\\n- **Operator review focus:** Review pass fourteen. First read `review/review-brief-14.txt` and follow it: it names the area by lineage label, the scope file, the graph and stop steps each iteration runs, and the holdout rule.\\n- **What the change did.** Six of the seven pass-thirteen intent signals were removed; only `vibe prompt hook` remains from that set. ADR-001 now waives AC-004 for P05, P08 and P09 and keeps their routes, and fixes P07 with `vibe prompt hook` alone.\\n- **What the review found.** The removal is correct and reproduces: the five prompts pass thirteen checked no longer top the advisor, and P05/P07/P08/P09 match ADR-001. It is not complete as a leak fix: four ordinary prompts still top the advisor through older generic signals, and ADR-001 does not record that residual.\\n- **Stop and recovery.** Iterations 1-2 covered all four dimensions. Iteration 3's stop was blocked because `checklist_evidence` was left `partial`; iteration 4 closed it but hit the two-pass stuck threshold. A recorded recovery pass swept one ordinary-sense prompt per remaining signal, found no new out-of-contract case, and the stop then converged.\\n- **Self-check outcomes.** F001 (P1) was confirmed by the full Hunter/Skeptic/Referee pass in iteration 1: each of the four prompts loses the advisor top-1 when only its matching signal is dropped. F002 (P2) was confirmed by reading ADR-001 beside the transcript it cites. No finding was downgraded or called a false positive.\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\n`/speckit:plan` is required: the verdict is CONDITIONAL on one active P1.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"triggered\\\": true,\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONDITIONAL\\\",\\n  \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": false,\\n  \\\"activeFindings\\\": [\\\"F001\\\", \\\"F002\\\"],\\n  \\\"remediationWorkstreams\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"WS-1\\\",\\n      \\\"findingIds\\\": [\\\"F001\\\"],\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P1\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Stop generic remaining intent signals from routing ordinary prompts\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": \\\"advisor intent_signals scoring surface: narrow which skill, route request, not offering a skill and workflow measure to advisor-specific compounds, or exclude their single tokens from the lexical lane; pin the four ordinary prompts as fixtures\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"WS-2\\\",\\n      \\\"findingIds\\\": [\\\"F002\\\"],\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Record the residual leak in the decision record and pin it\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": \\\"ADR-001 residual row or sentence plus a real-signal ordinary-sense fixture in the specificity test\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"specSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"State that an advisor intent signal must name advisor behaviour, not a word that appears in ordinary backend, career, HR or ops text.\\\",\\n    \\\"State that a leak check must cover every remaining generic signal, not only the phrases the current change added.\\\",\\n    \\\"State that a declined probe whose words were removed for leaking must be rechecked against the remaining surface.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"planSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Narrow which skill, route request, not offering a skill and workflow measure to advisor-specific compounds, and add the four ordinary prompts as negative fixtures.\\\",\\n    \\\"Add one ADR-001 row naming the residual generic signals and the reproducing prompts, and extend the specificity test with real-signal ordinary-sense cases.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"findingClasses\\\": [\\\"algorithmic\\\", \\\"matrix/evidence\\\"],\\n  \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/lexical.ts\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/declared-phrase-specificity.vitest.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/040-final-alignment-loop/decision-record.md\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": true\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n| ID | Severity | Dimension | Location | Finding | Fix recommendation | Finding class | Scope proof | Affected surface hints |\\n|----|----------|-----------|----------|---------|--------------------|---------------|-------------|------------------------|\\n| F001 | P1 | correctness | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json:70` | Four ordinary prompts top the advisor through pre-existing generic intent signals | Narrow which skill, route request, not offering a skill and workflow measure to advisor compounds, or exclude their single tokens; pin the four prompts | algorithmic | Each prompt returns `system-skill-advisor` 0.82 with the committed projection and loses the top-1 when only its matching signal is dropped; measure then returns `sk-design` | graph metadata, lexical lane, specificity test, after-pass-13 transcript |\\n| F002 | P2 | maintainability | `040-final-alignment-loop/decision-record.md:37` | ADR-001 records the pass-thirteen fix but not the residual leak it leaves open | Add a residual row naming the remaining generic signals and the four prompts, and pin them as fixtures | matrix/evidence | Read ADR-001 and the five-prompt transcript it cites; the test file pins fixture phrases only, so the residual is unpinned | decision record, tasks evidence, specificity test |\\n\\nImpact notes:\\n\\n- F001 changes the top recommendation for ordinary text: `route request to the backend service`, `which skill should I learn next as a developer`, `measure the workflow throughput` and `not offering a skill in the job listing` all lead with the advisor. No command is attached and no mutating command is offered.\\n- The four prompts pre-date the pass-thirteen change. F001 is a residual of the older surface, not a regression introduced by this diff.\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\n- **WS-1 (F001).** Treat the four generic signals as phrases only, or remove their single tokens from the lexical and derived lanes. Add the four prompts as ordinary-sense fixtures so the next phrase addition cannot silently regress. This is the same class pass thirteen fixed for the newly added phrases.\\n- **WS-2 (F002).** Record the residual in ADR-001 and extend the specificity test with real-signal ordinary-sense cases. The existing test builds a fixture projection and never reads the shipped signal list.\\n- No code change is made in this review. Both workstreams are planning seeds.\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- An advisor intent signal names advisor behaviour, not a word that appears in ordinary backend, career, HR or ops text.\\n- A leak check must cover every remaining generic signal, not only the phrases the current change added.\\n- A declined probe whose words were removed for leaking must be rechecked against the remaining surface.\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- Narrow the four generic signals to advisor-specific compounds and add the four ordinary prompts as negative fixtures.\\n- Add one ADR-001 row naming the residual signals and prompts, and extend the specificity test with real-signal ordinary-sense cases.\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | 5 | P05 returns `command-doctor-helper` with `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` first; P07 advisor; P08 `sk-doc`; P09 none; ADR-001 and the probe rows agree |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pass | 5 | AC-004, T006 and T008 carry evidence; F001 and F002 are the separately recorded residuals |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | 3 | Author metadata and the committed projection carry the same 33 canonical signals |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | 1 | No agent file or runtime-specific surface in this area |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | notApplicable | 2 | No feature catalog row changes in this area |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | 2 | No manual-testing playbook source in this area |\\n\\nAcceptance coverage: `AC_COVERAGE` is advisory only. AC-004 is waived by ADR-001 for P05, P08 and P09; AC-005 remains unmet pending this pass and the full alignment run. The advisory does not change the verdict.\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- F002 is advisory and can land with the F001 fix.\\n- The two ambiguous sweep cases, `route my request through the proxy` and `write a prompt-time brief for the team`, are recorded with F001's case set rather than as a separate finding. A later fix should decide whether `route my request` and `prompt-time brief` also need narrowing.\\n- T006's evidence cell records the earlier seven-phrase build. It is historical and superseded by T008 and ADR-001; no edit is requested here.\\n\\n## Dimension Expansion Map\\n\\n| Dimension | Iterations | Coverage |\\n|-----------|------------|----------|\\n| correctness | 1, 3, 4, 5 | complete |\\n| security | 2, 3, 4 | complete |\\n| traceability | 1, 3, 4, 5 | complete |\\n| maintainability | 2, 3, 4, 5 | complete |\\n\\n## 9. Search Ledger\\n\\n- Ordinary-sense sweep, correctness: four out-of-contract prompts found (`route request to the backend service`, `which skill should I learn next as a developer`, `measure the workflow throughput`, `not offering a skill in the job listing`), each proven by a single-signal drop test. Result: F001.\\n- Wider recovery sweep, correctness: thirteen further prompts tested; in-domain prompts (skill selection, scorer fusion, command transcripts, prompt hook health, private skills indexing, fallback scorer) route to the advisor by contract; ambiguous prompts (`route my request through the proxy`, `write a prompt-time brief for the team`) are added to F001's case set. No new finding.\\n- Pass-thirteen transcript replay: five prompts reproduce the recorded outcomes; four return no skill and one returns `system-spec-kit`.\\n- ADR and probe replay: P05 helper ranking, P07 pass, P08 `sk-doc`, P09 no skill. All match ADR-001.\\n- Holdout hygiene: both scope files and the cited transcript were checked for corpus references; none names `command-prompts.jsonl`, `holdout-prompts.jsonl` or `behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl`. No holdout row was read.\\n- Security pass: both files are static author text and markdown; 33 signals are unique, ASCII-only and metacharacter-free; no secret, host, credential or executable path.\\n\\n## 10. Audit Appendix\\n\\n- Iterations: 5. Iteration records were recorded through `append-mode-event.cjs`; the reducer refreshed the registry, dashboard and strategy after each.\\n- Convergence: stop reason `converged`, `composite_converged`, all nine legal-stop gates pass, `blockedBy` empty. One `stuckRecovery` was recorded after iteration 4 and the recovery pass was iteration 5.\\n- Verdict source: the findings registry (one P1, one P2). The iteration final lines are the leaf self-report; this report and the registry agree.\\n- Writes: confined to `review/lineages/data-14`. Review targets were read-only.\\n- Completion line: `FANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:data-14`.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794869451558,"end":1794869477455}}}}
