{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794869580989,"sessionID":"ses_e1984dae4ffewGkE5pBa89LndO","part":{"partID":"prt_1e69051cb0018MSK4VKuyGHvGY","sessionID":"ses_e1984dae4ffewGkE5pBa89LndO","messageID":"msg_1e6902484001Vm6K4XN2ilRFrL","type":"tool","id":"call_7b75a016009a4ff78cca464c","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/deep-review-strategy.md","offset":30,"limit":80},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/data-14/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 30-109\n30: ---\n31: \n32: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n33: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n34: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n35: [All dimensions complete]\n36: \n37: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n38: \n39: ---\n40: \n41: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n42: \n43: - Reviewing the mention area (`command-attach.ts` and its guard tests) assigned to `mention-14`; read-only context only.\n44: - Re-reporting the recorded limits in `review-brief-14.txt` unless a new input breaks them.\n45: - Re-reporting the open P2 list of `038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/alignment-final-dispositions.md` and of review passes ten to thirteen.\n46: - Running the repository suite, the build, or any git write; this lineage reports only.\n47: - Opening `command-prompts.jsonl`, `holdout-prompts.jsonl` or `behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl` except through the allowed aggregate path; the holdout rule stays in force.\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n52: \n53: - Composite convergence stop at threshold 0.10 with all four dimensions covered.\n54: - `maxIterations` 8 reached without a legal convergence stop.\n55: - A blocking stop from `convergence.cjs` naming an uncovered dimension or an unresolved active P0.\n56: \n57: ---\n58: \n59: ## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n60: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n61: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n62: - [x] correctness\n63: - [x] security\n64: - [x] traceability\n65: - [x] maintainability\n66: \n67: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: ## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n72: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n73: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n74: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n75: - P1 (Required): 1\n76: - P2 (Suggestions): 1\n77: - Resolved: 0\n78: \n79: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n80: \n81: ---\n82: \n83: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n84: \n85: - Init: reading the scope file, both diffs, then the whole files at `e626653ce79` before choosing a focus. It separated the phrase delta (six removed, one kept) from the ADR delta (three probes declined).\n86: - Iteration 1: scoring the ordinary prompts in-process with the committed projection, then dropping one signal at a time. The single-signal drop test separated a real signal match from a description or graph-edge effect and gave each P1 case a causal proof.\n87: - Iteration 1: reproducing the pass-thirteen leak transcript first, then widening it. The reproduction showed the removed phrases are clean and the residual lives in older signals.\n88: - Iteration 2: reading the cited leak transcript beside ADR-001. It showed the decision record's evidence is exactly the five prompts the removed phrases hit, which is why the residual went unrecorded.\n89: \n90: ---\n91: \n92: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n93: \n94: - Init: none.\n95: - Iteration 1: none. The first attempt at `doctor-helper-match.cjs` put the prompt before `--` and was rejected; the documented `--` form worked.\n96: \n97: ---\n98: \n99: ## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n100: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n101: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n102: ### A broader leak than F001 among the remaining signals: the wider sweep produced only in-domain or ambiguous results beyond the four established cases. -- BLOCKED (iteration 5, 1 attempts)\n103: - What was tried: A broader leak than F001 among the remaining signals: the wider sweep produced only in-domain or amb